<title>PORTUGAL: FORECAST - Portugal spreads seen steady on Bunds.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Portugal spreads seen steady on Bunds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the daily forecast for spreads in the Portuguese bond market based on a poll of four banks and one brokerage.</p>
<p>Poll covers spreads between the February 2007 Portuguese cash bond (OT) and the German and Spanish equivalents, together with the spreads between the Portuguese 10 and two-year bonds.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>			     Min spread Avge   Max  vs previous close</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs Bund July  07   66 bps   67.6  70	    68</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs Bono March 07    -5	-7.6  -9	    -7</p>
<p>						  YLDS3</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				 Min  Avge   Max</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs March 99	 119  121.2  125     vs     119</p>
<p>						  PT/CURVE</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Key factors likely to affect market:</p>
<p>-The 10-years seen trading calmly. The curve remains well-supported in the short to medium sector although no great steepening envisaged.</p>
<p>--Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
